TITLE:: PianoRollSidebar
SUMMARY:: Right-docked sidebar showing loop length and selection count for the piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollSidebar:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: fixed to the right edge of LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: (sibling of the roll LINK::Classes/ScrollView::, not inside the scroll canvas). It displays the loop length from LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: when a loop has been defined (both start and end markers have been set), and the number of selected notes. The loop length is hidden until a loop is defined.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollSidebar::.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for label colours.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: refresh
Updates the selection label and the loop-length display.

ARGUMENT:: selectionCount
Number of currently selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

ARGUMENT:: loopLength
Loop length in beats, or CODE::nil:: when no loop is defined. When CODE::nil::, the loop heading and value are hidden.

PRIVATE:: init, prFormatLoopLength
